{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"compacted_at":1788424616667267001,"compiled_state":{"alias":"climactic-deistic-bagworm","assignee":null,"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","authorship":{"signed":3,"unsigned":0},"authorship_ledger":[{"content_hash":"e1f9be838c9c6801b84cef8a6d9d8984f1d7b2e54978adb7ae42fccd3d83b352","event_uuid":"31974b0d-5732-4df1-8794-10a19ab7b550","position":{"commit_sha":"0e8f560435b014b9d508d809368bb65e46ce5f7a","position":"1788421647151960001-31974b0d-5732-4df1-8794-10a19ab7b550"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"0a31822fc43597777039590868f99a8787f6282c9f1d78e6c36312c639093569","event_uuid":"b94c0bc4-63e2-4b03-98fb-4ee78818cbf4","position":{"commit_sha":"4f68b5973ceb2765db9a3bb2e91033a70898d951","position":"1788421653234101001-b94c0bc4-63e2-4b03-98fb-4ee78818cbf4"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"cbe046695c62a51748890bab89d1223b6d7c6530f9a21b8a94e7a266bd2668b7","event_uuid":"1985bb1f-f6d0-469f-99e3-4b08409ec8f4","position":{"commit_sha":"56769b36fc6be46622eea03b7c83350110a91eb6","position":"1788421678368595001-1985bb1f-f6d0-469f-99e3-4b08409ec8f4"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[],"created_at":1788421647151960001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"1985bb1f-f6d0-469f-99e3-4b08409ec8f4","relation":"depends_on","target_id":"7370-0274-9f80-437d"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\n\nOnce 038d retires the eight old env/config spellings, the published docs and generated reference surfaces must stop presenting them as live aliases. The single-leaf plan review also identified generated/tested surfaces that pin the old names: `docs/env-vars.md`, `tests/unit/test_gen_env_registry.py`, `tests/golden/config_surface.json`, and `tests/unit/test_config_surface_golden.py`.\n\n## Approach\n\nAfter the ADR and runtime children land, regenerate or update every published config/env reference so only canonical spellings remain in live guidance. Keep clearly dated historical references only where they are intentional archival records, and make the release/changelog text name each removed spelling and its canonical replacement. Re-run the full token census so any residual old-name occurrence is classified as either a tombstone/error test, the new ADR, or a clearly historical record.\n\n## Scope\n\n- `docs/env-vars.md`, `docs/config.md`, `docs/config-reference.md`, `docs/bash-migration.md`, `docs/concurrency.md`, `docs/api-stability.md`, `docs/release-notes.md`, `CHANGELOG.md`\n- `tests/unit/test_gen_env_registry.py`, `tests/unit/test_config_surface_golden.py`, and `tests/golden/config_surface.json`\n- any generator or helper invoked to regenerate those published surfaces\n\n## Testing\n\nRun the exact generator/regeneration commands for the env-var and config-surface outputs, prove the updated tests pass, and run a complete-population string sweep across the eight retired spellings to confirm only intentional tombstone/history references remain.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] Live documentation and examples use only canonical spellings for the eight removed env/config names.\n- [ ] Generated env/config reference surfaces and their tests are regenerated so they no longer present the old names as live aliases.\n- [ ] Release/changelog documentation names every removal and its canonical replacement.\n- [ ] A full string census of the eight removed spellings leaves only intentional tombstones, the new ADR, or clearly historical references.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":"docs/env-vars.md","reason":"remove live alias rows from generated env docs"},{"path":"docs/config.md","reason":"replace live alias guidance with canonical-only text"},{"path":"docs/config-reference.md","reason":"remove verify.overlap_enabled alias documentation"},{"path":"docs/bash-migration.md","reason":"remove live REBAR_NO_SYNC alias guidance"},{"path":"docs/concurrency.md","reason":"remove live REBAR_NO_SYNC alias guidance"},{"path":"docs/api-stability.md","reason":"align published stability guidance with the ADR"},{"path":"docs/release-notes.md","reason":"record the alias removals and replacements"},{"path":"CHANGELOG.md","reason":"record the alias removals and replacements"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_gen_env_registry.py","reason":"update env-registry expectations after alias retirement"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_config_surface_golden.py","reason":"update config-surface golden expectations"},{"path":"tests/golden/config_surface.json","reason":"regenerate the config-surface golden without verify.overlap_enabled"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"managed_refs":[["depends_on","7370-0274-9f80-437d"],["parent","038d-f5ff-b371-4ba5"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"038d-f5ff-b371-4ba5","parent_status_uuid":"","plan_review_phase":"planning","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"open","tags":["janitor","config","breaking-change","compatibility"],"ticket_id":"1a63-056e-98b9-4ab7","ticket_type":"task","title":"Publish canonical config removal docs","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["31974b0d-5732-4df1-8794-10a19ab7b550","b94c0bc4-63e2-4b03-98fb-4ee78818cbf4","1985bb1f-f6d0-469f-99e3-4b08409ec8f4"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1788424616667267001,"uuid":"18fbb0f7-c9f4-4f89-8c62-7f60c6339c10"}